e2e.evidence:
npx playwright test --project=chromium --project=api, development mode: 103 passed / 14 skipped, 0 failed, 1.9m -- up from 93/14, the ten new tests being player-controls.spec.ts. Run again after this round's changes to the control bar, not only before them.

THE TEN, AND WHY EACH IS HERE RATHER THAN IN A UNIT TEST. apps/web has no DOM, so a keyboard clause tested without a keyboard is not tested:
  - every control the acceptance names is on the page and has an accessible name;
  - THE NATIVE VIDEO CHROME IS GONE -- two seek bars that disagree about the position is worse than one;
  - the whole bar is reachable with TAB, in order, with nothing skipped;
  - SPACE operates the player AND DOES NOT SCROLL THE PAGE;
  - the arrow keys move the volume rather than the page;
  - M mutes and the button says which state it is in;
  - a track menu opens, announces itself, and says so when there is nothing to choose;
  - ESCAPE closes the menu;
  - THE BAR NEVER LEAVES THE ACCESSIBILITY TREE, however it is dimmed -- which is the acceptance clause "an idle-hide overlay that never hides a control from a keyboard or screen-reader user", and is why the idle state is opacity rather than display:none, visibility:hidden, aria-hidden or inert, each of which would remove the controls from the tree or the keyboard;
  - the seek bar announces a TIME rather than a percentage.

WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT ASSERTED, AND THE REASON MATTERS MORE THAN THE OMISSION: THAT THE PICTURE MOVES. The demo catalog's sources are fixtures and no real media decodes in this harness, so a test that clicked Play and waited for `playing` would be asserting the fixture rather than the control. What a command reaching the adapter looks like is covered in the adapter's own suite; what a viewer can OPERATE is covered here.

NOT COVERED BY ANY SUITE, AND STATED RATHER THAN LEFT TO BE FOUND: the re-application of a viewer's track choice across a real candidate switch, end to end in a browser. The DECISION has 11 unit tests and four caught mutations, and the wiring that issues it is three lines in one event branch -- but no harness in this repository produces two candidates with real track lists, because no real media decodes here. It is honest unit coverage of the rule plus unverified wiring of the issue, and it is the first thing to exercise when a real stream exists.
